{"nodes": [{"id": "vault_adr_0204_glue_home_mixes_the_set_decision", "label": "ADR 0204: GLUE Home mixes the set whenever it runs: the website's mixer ported to Rust, streamed to the tab", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "vault/adr/0204-glue-home-mixes-the-set.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The user (2026-11-27): remote use is slow because the browser downloads every song whole to mix it; GLUE Home should process and stream instead. The browser decoded about 100 MB per song and mixed at about 67x real time. There is no licence in the repo, so LAME (LGPL) cannot be linked into GLUE Home; the tab's MP3 encoder stays. Raw PCM over the local link was chosen over a codec (352 KB/s on 127.0.0.1, exact). Remotely, Opus is for listening and FLAC for a file, deferred to its own ADR."}, {"id": "vault_adr_0204_glue_sets_crate", "label": "glue-sets: the set mixer ported to Rust (crates/glue-sets)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/adr/0204-glue-home-mixes-the-set.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "src/core/sets/{tempo,dsp,automation,mixer}.ts ported line for line, with JavaScript's numbers (f64, f32 where stored, glue_audio::js for Math). Held to the TypeScript by tests/golden/sets: fixed plans from exact arithmetic, every 256th frame within 1e-6. About 200x real time for two key-locked decks."}, {"id": "vault_adr_0204_set_sessions", "label": "Set sessions in GLUE Home's engine: setOpen, setPlan, setClose", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/adr/0204-glue-home-mixes-the-set.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Songs are read at a player's priority so the analysis gives way. Songs due in the next 20 s are decoded ahead and four more are kept for seeking back. Sessions idle for 30 minutes are let go."}, {"id": "vault_adr_0204_pcm_stream", "label": "Local link GET /set/<id>/pcm: the mix as stereo f32 at 44.1 kHz", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/adr/0204-glue-home-mixes-the-set.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chunked from a bounded channel, so a reader that stops holds the renderer back and a reader that goes away stops it."}, {"id": "vault_adr_0204_remote_next", "label": "Remote set streaming (next: Opus to listen, FLAC for a file)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/adr/0204-glue-home-mixes-the-set.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same sessions over a device's connection; the mix sent as Opus (about 192 kbps) for listening and as FLAC for a file, which the device writes as WAV or MP3 itself. Its own ADR will follow."}, {"id": "src_lib_sets_home", "label": "HomeSet: the website's client of GLUE Home's set mixer (src/lib/sets/home.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/adr/0204-glue-home-mixes-the-set.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_workers_setplay_worker", "label": "Set preview worker (src/workers/setplay.worker.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/adr/0204-glue-home-mixes-the-set.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_workers_mixdown_worker", "label": "Set export worker (src/workers/mixdown.worker.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/adr/0204-glue-home-mixes-the-set.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tests_sets_golden_test", "label": "Set goldens recorder (tests/sets.golden.test.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/adr/0204-glue-home-mixes-the-set.md"